      "answer": "The search results already returned the full rulebook text for *Brittle*. No additional tool calls are needed — the definition is fully present in the verified results.\n\n---\n\n## Brittle — Frosthaven Condition\n\n> **Brittle:** The next time the figure would suffer damage from any source, they instead suffer double that amount of damage, and Brittle is then removed. Brittle is also removed if the figure is healed.\n\n*(Frosthaven Rulebook, Negative Conditions section)*\n\n---\n\n### Key Points\n\n- **Doubles the next damage taken** — from any source, including *Wound*, environmental effects, or attacks.\n- **Single-use:** It is removed immediately after that doubled damage is applied.\n- **Healing also removes it** — so a figure can \"cure\" *Brittle* by being healed before taking damage.\n- ***Ward* interaction:** If a figure has both *Ward* and *Brittle* when they suffer damage, the two conditions **negate each other** and both are removed — the damage is neither doubled nor halved.\n- *Brittle* is a **negative condition** and follows all standard negative condition rules (e.g., enemies are immune to conditions their ability cards don't grant).",
